  "notes": "そっち is a casual pronoun meaning \"that way\" or \"there\" - referring to a place near the listener.\n\nKO-SO-A-DO SERIES (〜っち forms):\n- こっち: this way (near speaker)\n- そっち: that way (near listener)\n- あっち: over there (away from both)\n- どっち: which way (question)\n\nFORMALITY LEVELS:\n- そっち: casual/informal\n- そちら: polite/formal\n\nMEANINGS:\n1. Direction/place: そっちに{行|い}って (Go that way)\n2. That one: そっちにしよう (Let's go with that one)\n3. Listener's side: そっちはどう？ (How are things on your end?)\n\nNOTE:\nOften used in phone calls or messages: そっちの{天気|てんき}は？ (How's the weather there?)",
